{title: Line of Perez}
{subtitle: 1 Chronicles 2:4–5; Ruth 4:18–20; Matthew 1:3–4; Luke 3:32–33}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [C] | [Bb] | ×2
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Tamar bore Perez and Zerah
Judah [C]had five sons in all
Hez[Bb]ron and Hamul were his sons
The [A]line begins to stand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Perez [Dm]father of Hezron
Hezron [C]father of Ram
Ram [Bb]father of Amminadab
[Gm]Amminadab father of [Dm]Nahshon
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Nahshon father of Salmon
[C]Salmon link in the chain
[Bb]Boaz Obed Jesse
[A]Jesse son of David
The [Dm]name Shamhuth is hidden
[C]In the scroll of Ruth
From [Bb]Perez to the king
The [A]bloodline stands
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Dm] | [Bb] | [C] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]Luke traces back to Adam
[C]Matthew follows the king
[Bb]Through the generations passed
The [A]promise holds its ground
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Salmon of [Dm]Nahshon
[C]Nahshon of [Bb]Amminadab
[Gm]The line of Judah en[Dm]dures [C]
In the book of [Bb]life
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Bb] | [Gm] | [Dm] | [C] |
| [Bb] | [Gm] | [Gm] |
